<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herceg Novi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herceg Novi is a fortified port at the entrance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-kotor">Bay of Kotor</a> in present-day Montenegro. Founded as Novi in 1382 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko I of Bosnia</a>, it was developed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stjepan-vukcic-kosaca">Stjepan Vukčić Kosača</a>, Herceg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-sava">Saint Sava</a>, whose title gave the town its name. It fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1482 and later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1687.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herceg-novi.jpg" alt="Herceg Novi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zlatko at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herceg_Novi_Sunset.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
